            <ArticleTitle>Association study of polymorphisms within matrix metalloproteinase 9 with bronchial asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>233-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Matrix metalloproteinase 9 plays an important role in the development of bronchial asthma. We were interested in whether the polymorphisms -T1702A, -C1562T, R279Q and +C6T within the matrix metalloproteinase 9 (MMP-9) gene were associated with asthma in a population of 231 asthmatic children. However, we found no association. Thus MMP-9 might not be a major gene for asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
